%description:

Tcp.mss:invalid -- an MSS below 88 stops the run with an error.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "else at least 88 (Linux TCP_MIN_MSS)".

The classes: auto (-1, the default), with a facet for IPv4 and one for IPv6; explicit (88 and
more); invalid (0 to 87, and below -1). The code: TcpConnection::initConnection() and
resolveAddressFamilyMss().

Host under test: host1. Observation: the error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.mss
%# class: invalid
%# value: 87
%# key: *.host1.tcp.mss
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpMssInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.mss = 87    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
mss must be -1 or at least 88, but it is 87
